    "body": "Fixes #8103\n\nIterating over a literal sequence whose items have different types, such as `(123, 123.45)` or `[True, 2]`, coerced all items to a common C type and changed the type or value of the loop variable.  Single-character bytes literals were also inferred as C characters, so `for c in [b'a', b'b']` produced integers instead of bytes objects\n\nOnly infer an item type when all items have the same type, and keep single-character bytes literals as bytes objects.  Single-character `str` literals still iterate over `Py_UCS4`, which converts back to `str`\n\nNew and updated tests are in `tests/run/type_inference.pyx` and `tests/run/for_in_iter.py`\n",
    "closed_at": null,
