                "message": "Fix type inference for iteration over literal sequences with mixed item types (GH-8103)\n\nIterating over a literal sequence whose items have different types, such as\n(123, 123.45) or [True, 2], could coerce all items to a common C type and\nchange the type or value of the loop variable.  Single-character bytes\nliterals were inferred as C characters, so looping over [b'a', b'b'] produced\nintegers instead of bytes objects.\n\nOnly infer an item type if all items have the same type and keep\nsingle-character bytes literals as bytes objects.  Single-character string\nliterals still iterate over Py_UCS4, which converts back to str.",
